    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n89352" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">προσ-ζεύγνῡμι</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>attach by a yoke</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ ἄροτρον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Porph.
					<u>Abst.</u>
					2.30
				</span></i>
			: metaph., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῇ ὕλῃ τὸν τεχνίτην προσέζευξεν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Placit.</u>
					1.3.5
				</span></i>
			:—more freq. in 
				Pass.
			, <i>to be yoked, harnessed to</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τινι</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Ner.</u>
				4
			</span></i>: abs., <i>to be attached</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ᾗ τὸ πηδάλιον προσέζευκται</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>Mech.</u>
					851a33
				</span></i>
			: metaph., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῷ προσέζευξαι
			πλάνῳ</span>; <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Alc.</u>
				482
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Plot.
				1.4.16
			</span></i>; <i>to be contiguous</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πύργοις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					J.
					<u>BJ</u>
					5.4.4
				</span></i>
			.</div>
